# Restore pointer DPI for the mirrors rebinded creates.
#
# Claiming a wheel means claiming the pointer it belongs to, so rebinded
# replays that pointer through a uinput mirror. 70-mouse.rules builds its hwdb
# key as "mouse:$env{ID_BUS}:v...p...:name:...", and ID_BUS is derived from the
# USB parent device. A uinput device has no USB parent, so the key comes out as
# "mouse::v..." instead of "mouse:usb:v...", never matches, and the mouse ends
# up with no MOUSE_DPI. libinput then accelerates against a default 1000 DPI
# rather than the real one, which is felt directly as the wrong sensitivity.
#
# Running the same lookup with the bus spelled out gives the mirror the DPI its
# source would have been given. The match is limited to virtual input devices
# that report a USB bustype, which is what a mirror of a USB pointer looks like.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", \
  DEVPATH=="*/virtual/input/*", ATTRS{id/bustype}=="0003", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}=="1", \
  IMPORT{builtin}="hwdb 'mouse:usb:v$attr{id/vendor}p$attr{id/product}:name:$attr{name}:'"
